00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:22.920
Speaker 2: And that is why I think we all ought to be passionate about subject matters like this.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:31.240
Speaker 2: Now just to wrap this up, let's talk about how do we witness to this people group.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:44.200
Speaker 2: One of the core things that we must do is that you must understand that many of the African traditional adherents have been sold lies about Christianity.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.770
Speaker 2: Yes, several lies.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.650
Speaker 2: A lot of them don't.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:57.050
Speaker 2: Some of them, you will meet some of them who claim that I used to be a Christian, but I stopped being a Christian.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.010
Speaker 2: But when you start to engage them, you realize this person was never saved.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:06.290
Speaker 2: You attended church, you did a couple of practices, but you never heard the gospel.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.530
Speaker 1: You never heard the gospel what the gospel is.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:24.359
Speaker 2: And so one of the things that you must be armed with is defending the core doctrines of Christianity, knowing how to even explain it to someone who has not heard it before.

00:02:25.239 --> 00:02:31.479
Speaker 2: So lies about Jesus, lies about God, lies about the Bible.

00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:35.799
Speaker 2: The Bible was written by men, so it can't be trusted.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.690
Speaker 2: Things like that, the Bible has been corrupted.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:43.450
Speaker 2: Things like that we mentioned earlier that was still going to be addressed next week.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.690
Speaker 2: I think you should look forward to that.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:46.210
Speaker 1: It will be a packed one.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:46.930
Speaker 2: Exactly.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.090
Speaker 2: So I think you must be armed with that.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.890
Speaker 2: The next thing I think you must do is that you must answer some of their genuine concerns.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:58.450
Speaker 2: For example, PDAMs, have you heard someone say that Christianity is a white man's religion?

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.050
Speaker 1: You know, that was just in my mind while you were speaking.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:11.280
Speaker 1: And it's a triggering point for us who are at least on this side, if you are from the Audience where we are speaking from practically Nigerians or Africans, you begin to.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.960
Speaker 1: There's a sense of comrade that comes with it.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:23.480
Speaker 1: And because of all the things that we seem to associate with the era of colonialism and all of that, we begin to associate the same feeling with this.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.960
Speaker 1: And there's a sense of rebellion.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:25.440
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.520
Speaker 1: It's a white man's religion.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.760
Speaker 1: We had our own religion.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.120
Speaker 1: So why is this the case?

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.840
Speaker 1: Blah, blah, blah.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.680
